              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2024-5535?s=redhat&n=openssl&ns=redhat&t=rpm&osn=redhatlinux&osv=8&vr=%3C1%3A1.1.1k-14.el8_6",
              "help": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in OpenSSL. Affected versions of this package are vulnerable to Information Exposure through the SSL_select_next_proto function. This flaw allows an attacker to cause unexpected application behavior or a crash by exploiting the buffer overread condition when the function is called with a zero-length client list. This issue is only exploitable if the application is misconfigured to use a zero-length server list and mishandles the 'no overlap' response in ALPN or uses the output as the opportunistic protocol in NPN.\n",
                "markdown": "> A flaw was found in OpenSSL. Affected versions of this package are vulnerable to Information Exposure through the SSL_select_next_proto function. This flaw allows an attacker to cause unexpected application behavior or a crash by exploiting the buffer overread condition when the function is called with a zero-length client list. This issue is only exploitable if the application is misconfigured to use a zero-length server list and mishandles the 'no overlap' response in ALPN or uses the output as the opportunistic protocol in NPN.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                           |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:rpm/redhat/openssl@1%3A1.1.1k-9.el8_7?os_name=redhatlinux&os_version=8  |\n|Affected range                                                                 <1:1.1.1k-14.el8_6                                                          |\n|Fixed version                                                                  1:1.1.1k-14.el8_6                                                           |\n|[[CVSS Score 5.9] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H]]                                                                              |\n"
