              "help": {
                "text": "A double-free vulnerability has been discovered in glibc (GNU C Library). This flaw occurs during bracket expression parsing within the regcomp function, specifically when a memory allocation failure takes place. Exploitation of a double-free vulnerability can lead to memory corruption, which could enable an attacker to achieve arbitrary code execution or a denial of service condition.\n",
                "markdown": "> A double-free vulnerability has been discovered in glibc (GNU C Library). This flaw occurs during bracket expression parsing within the regcomp function, specifically when a memory allocation failure takes place. Exploitation of a double-free vulnerability can lead to memory corruption, which could enable an attacker to achieve arbitrary code execution or a denial of service condition.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                   |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:rpm/redhat/glibc@2.28-211.el8?os_name=redhatlinux&os_version=8  |\n|Affected range                                                                 <2.28-251.el8_10.25                                                 |\n|Fixed version                                                                  2.28-251.el8_10.25                                                  |\n|[[CVSS Score 4.2] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L]]                                                                      |\n"
