              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-22365: Insecure Inherited Permissions"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2024-22365?s=redhat&n=pam&ns=redhat&t=rpm&osn=redhatlinux&osv=8&vr=%3C1.3.1-33.el8",
              "help": {
                "text": "A vulnerability was found in Linux PAM. An unprivileged user that is not yet in a corresponding mount namespace with ~/tmp mounted as a polyinstantiated dir can place a FIFO there, and a subsequent attempt to login as this user with `pam_namespace` configured will cause the `openat()` in `protect_dir()` to block the attempt, causing a local denial of service.\n",
                "markdown": "> A vulnerability was found in Linux PAM. An unprivileged user that is not yet in a corresponding mount namespace with ~/tmp mounted as a polyinstantiated dir can place a FIFO there, and a subsequent attempt to login as this user with `pam_namespace` configured will cause the `openat()` in `protect_dir()` to block the attempt, causing a local denial of service.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                 |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:rpm/redhat/pam@1.3.1-22.el8?os_name=redhatlinux&os_version=8  |\n|Affected range                                                                 <1.3.1-33.el8                                                     |\n|Fixed version                                                                  1.3.1-33.el8                                                      |\n|[[CVSS Score 5.5] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H]]                                                                    |\n"
