              "id": "CVE-2025-13281",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-13281: Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-13281?s=github&n=kubernetes&ns=k8s.io&t=golang&vr=%3C1.32.10",
              "help": {
                "text": "A half-blind Server Side Request Forgery (SSRF) vulnerability exists in kube-controller-manager when using the in-tree Portworx StorageClass. This vulnerability allows authorized users to leak arbitrary information from unprotected endpoints in the control plane’s host network (including link-local or loopback services).\n",
                "markdown": "> A half-blind Server Side Request Forgery (SSRF) vulnerability exists in kube-controller-manager when using the in-tree Portworx StorageClass. This vulnerability allows authorized users to leak arbitrary information from unprotected endpoints in the control plane’s host network (including link-local or loopback services).\n\n|                                                                                                                    |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:golang/k8s.io/kubernetes@1.25.6  |\n|Affected range                                                                 <1.32.10                             |\n|Fixed version                                                                  1.32.10                              |\n|[[CVSS Score 5.8] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:H/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:N/A:N]]                                       |\n"
