            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-29406",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-29406"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2023-29406?s=golang&n=stdlib&t=golang&vr=%3C1.19.11",
              "help": {
                "text": "The HTTP/1 client does not fully validate the contents of the Host header. A maliciously crafted Host header can inject additional headers or entire requests.\n\nWith fix, the HTTP/1 client now refuses to send requests containing an invalid Request.Host or Request.URL.Host value.\n",
                "markdown": "> The HTTP/1 client does not fully validate the contents of the Host header. A maliciously crafted Host header can inject additional headers or entire requests.\n\nWith fix, the HTTP/1 client now refuses to send requests containing an invalid Request.Host or Request.URL.Host value.\n\n|                                          |\n|Package         pkg:golang/stdlib@1.19.7  |\n|Affected range  <1.19.11                  |\n|Fixed version   1.19.11                   |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<1.19.11",
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
                "fixed_version": "1.19.11",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.19.7"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.5",
                "tags": [
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-4527",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-4527: Stack-based Buffer Overflow"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2023-4527?s=redhat&n=glibc&ns=redhat&t=rpm&osn=redhatlinux&osv=8&vr=%3C2.28-225.el8_8.6",
              "help": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in glibc. When the getaddrinfo function is called with the AF_UNSPEC address family and the system is configured with no-aaaa mode via /etc/resolv.conf, a DNS response via TCP larger than 2048 bytes can potentially disclose stack contents through the function returned address data, and may cause a crash.\n",
                "markdown": "> A flaw was found in glibc. When the getaddrinfo function is called with the AF_UNSPEC address family and the system is configured with no-aaaa mode via /etc/resolv.conf, a DNS response via TCP larger than 2048 bytes can potentially disclose stack contents through the function returned address data, and may cause a crash.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                   |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:rpm/redhat/glibc@2.28-211.el8?os_name=redhatlinux&os_version=8  |\n|Affected range                                                                 <2.28-225.el8_8.6                                                   |\n|Fixed version                                                                  2.28-225.el8_8.6                                                    |\n|[[CVSS Score 6.5] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:H]]                                                                      |\n"
              },
