              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-4802?s=redhat&n=glibc&ns=redhat&t=rpm&osn=redhatlinux&osv=8&vr=%3C2.28-251.el8_10.22",
              "help": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in the glibc library. A statically linked setuid binary that calls dlopen(), including internal dlopen() calls after setlocale() or calls to NSS functions such as getaddrinfo(), may incorrectly search LD_LIBRARY_PATH to determine which library to load, allowing a local attacker to load malicious shared libraries, escalate privileges and execute arbitrary code.\n",
                "markdown": "> A flaw was found in the glibc library. A statically linked setuid binary that calls dlopen(), including internal dlopen() calls after setlocale() or calls to NSS functions such as getaddrinfo(), may incorrectly search LD_LIBRARY_PATH to determine which library to load, allowing a local attacker to load malicious shared libraries, escalate privileges and execute arbitrary code.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                   |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:rpm/redhat/glibc@2.28-211.el8?os_name=redhatlinux&os_version=8  |\n|Affected range                                                                 <2.28-251.el8_10.22                                                 |\n|Fixed version                                                                  2.28-251.el8_10.22                                                  |\n|[[CVSS Score 7.0] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H]]                                                                      |\n"
