              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2024-10963?s=redhat&n=pam&ns=redhat&t=rpm&osn=redhatlinux&osv=8&vr=%3C1.3.1-36.el8_10",
              "help": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in pam_access, where certain rules in its configuration file are mistakenly treated as hostnames. This vulnerability allows attackers to trick the system by pretending to be a trusted hostname, gaining unauthorized access. This issue poses a risk for systems that rely on this feature to control who can access certain services or terminals.\n",
