              "id": "CVE-2023-4911",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-4911: Heap-based Buffer Overflow"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2023-4911?s=redhat&n=glibc&ns=redhat&t=rpm&osn=redhatlinux&osv=8&vr=%3C2.28-225.el8_8.6",
              "help": {
                "text": "A buffer overflow was discovered in the GNU C Library's dynamic loader ld.so while processing the GLIBC_TUNABLES environment variable. This issue could allow a local attacker to use maliciously crafted GLIBC_TUNABLES environment variables when launching binaries with SUID permission to execute code with elevated privileges.\n",
