            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-22184",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-22184: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-22184?s=redhat&n=zlib&ns=redhat&t=rpm&osn=redhatlinux&osv=8&vr=%3E%3D0",
              "help": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in zlib. A global buffer overflow vulnerability exists in the `untgz` utility, specifically within the `TGZfname()` function. This flaw allows an attacker to provide an archive name longer than 1024 bytes, leading to an out-of-bounds write. This can result in memory corruption, denial of service, and potentially arbitrary code execution on the affected system.\n",
                "markdown": "> A flaw was found in zlib. A global buffer overflow vulnerability exists in the `untgz` utility, specifically within the `TGZfname()` function. This flaw allows an attacker to provide an archive name longer than 1024 bytes, leading to an out-of-bounds write. This can result in memory corruption, denial of service, and potentially arbitrary code execution on the affected system.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                     |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:rpm/redhat/zlib@1.2.11-21.el8_7?os_name=redhatlinux&os_version=8  |\n|Affected range                                                                 >=0                                                                   |\n|Fixed version                                                                  not fixed                                                             |\n|[[CVSS Score 8.6] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:H]]                                                                        |\n"
